oP) position to gain a comprehensive view of India's economic health."},{"question":"What is the significance of the Net Inflows - Services Trade data  ?","answer":"The balance of services trade reflects global demand for Indian services, global competitiveness, technological advancements, and India's integration into the global economy.^Net inflows in services trade data helps in assessing the effectiveness of trade policies, bilateral agreements, and other strategic initiatives aimed at promoting service exports or managing service imports.^Trends in net inflows can provide insights into global market dynamics, demand for Indian services abroad, and domestic demand for foreign services."}],"related":[{"slug":"baltic-dry-index","title":"Baltic Dry Index"},{"slug":"crude-oil-price-indian-basket","title":"Crude Oil Price (Indian Basket)"},{"slug":"external-commercial-borrowings-ecbs","title":"External Commercial Borrowings (ECBs)"},{"slug":"foreign-exchange-reserves","title":"Foreign Exchange Reserves"},{"slug":"foreign-tourist-arrivals","title":"Foreign Tourist Arrivals"},{"slug":"gross-foreign-direct-investment-fdi","title":"Gross Foreign Direct Investment (FDI)"},{"slug":"gross-foreign-portfolio-investment-fpi","title":"Gross Foreign Portfolio Investment (FPI)"},{"slug":"import-cover-months","title":"Import Cover (Months)"},{"slug":"international-air-passenger-traffic","title":"Air Passenger Traffic - International"},{"slug":"non-oil-exports","title":"Non-Oil Exports"},{"slug":"port-cargo-traffic","title":"Port Cargo Traffic"}],"title":"Services Trade- Net Inflows","description":"India's net services trade inflows stand at $ 16,910 Million for Sep 2026. India runs a consistent services surplus, driven largely by IT exports.","headline":{"Absolute":"India's net services trade inflows stand at $ 16,910 Million for Sep 2026. India runs a consistent services surplus, driven largely by IT exports.","Y-o-Y":"India's net services trade inflows stand at -10.20% for Sep 20